# Documentation stays local — it is not synced to GitHub.
# The files below remain on disk and keep being read by the checklists,
# the portal and the agents; they are simply no longer tracked. What is
# already in the repository's history is still there: this stops future
# commits from carrying them, it does not unpublish what was pushed.
# `scripts/check_docs_layout.py`, `check_docs_coverage.py` and
# `generate_catalogs.py --check` still run by hand; their CI jobs are
# commented out in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` because a fresh checkout
# has no `docs/` for them to read.
/docs/
/CHANGELOG.md
/CLAUDE.md
/frontend/CHANGELOG.md
backend/app/modules/*/CLAUDE.md
backend/app/modules/*/CHANGELOG.md
backend/app/modules/*/README.md
backend/app/modules/catalog/reference/README.md
backend/app/core/plugins/README.md
# `frontend/README.md` is not here on purpose: it is the Nuxt starter's
# boilerplate, not documentation of ours. `backend/pyproject.toml`
# declares `readme = "README.md"`, so do not add a rule that would catch
# a `backend/README.md` someone writes for it.

# Jenkins local
/jenkins-local/

# CodeGraph local index (regenerable with `codegraph init`)
/.codegraph/
